body:
`ObjectManagerPage` duplicated most of `MetadataManagerPage`/`MetadataDetailPage` logic. This removes it entirely and routes all object management through the generic metadata pipeline.

### New extension point: `listComponent`

Added `listComponent` to `MetadataTypeConfig` — when set, `MetadataManagerPage` delegates the entire list body to the custom component while still rendering the page shell (header, back button, title).

```typescript
export interface MetadataTypeConfig {
  // ...existing fields...
  listComponent?: React.ComponentType<MetadataListComponentProps>;
}

export interface MetadataListComponentProps {
  config: MetadataTypeConfig;
  basePath: string;
  metadataType: string;
  isAdmin: boolean;
}
```

### Object type registry config

```typescript
{
  type: 'object',
  label: 'Object',
  pluralLabel: 'Object Manager',
  // customRoute removed — now uses standard /system/metadata/object
  pageSchemaFactory: (itemName, item) => buildObjectDetailPageSchema(itemName, item),
  listComponent: ObjectManagerListAdapter,
}
```

### What changed

- **`ObjectManagerListAdapter`** — new component wrapping `ObjectManager` from `@object-ui/plugin-designer`, wired to MetadataService CRUD with optimistic update + rollback
- **`MetadataManagerPage`** — renders `listComponent` when configured, before the default card/grid branch
- **Routes** — `/system/objects` → `<Navigate>` redirect to `/system/metadata/object`; detail routes use `ObjectRedirect` helper to preserve `:objectName` param
- **Entry points** — sidebar, QuickActions, SystemHubPage hub cards all point to `/system/metadata/object`
- **Deleted** — `ObjectManagerPage.tsx`, its test file
- **Tests** — migrated to `ObjectManagerMetadataPipeline.test.tsx` covering list (via MetadataManagerPage) and detail (via MetadataDetailPage) paths; updated registry and detail page test assertions
